{"id": "EUVD-2026-102973", "enisaUuid": "5a7b170f-9c44-3059-b7f7-fc032ae0c222", "description": "EFAK 5.0.0 through 5.1.0 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows authenticated low-privilege users to read LLM provider API keys through the /api/model-config REST API. Attackers with any ROLE_USER account can query /api/model-config/page or /api/model-config/{id} to retrieve unmasked keys, enabling provider account access and incurred costs.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:04:04", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/efak-missing-admin-gate-user-management-api", "https://github.com/smartloli/EFAK/blob/v5.1.0/efak-web/src/main/java/org/kafka/eagle/web/controller/ModelConfigController.java#L34-L56", "https://github.com/smartloli/EFAK/blob/v5.1.0/efak-web/src/main/java/org/kafka/eagle/web/security/config/WebSecurityConfig.java#L89-L93", "https://github.com/smartloli/EFAK", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/efak-5.0.0-through-5.1.0-missing-authorization-via-api-model-config-exposes-api-keys"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jqpg-p8wq-hcmv", "CVE-2026-111682"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.39, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c64408d5-b53e-3038-ae36-4d2976d899a7", "product": {"name": "EFAK", "vendor": {"name": "smartloli"}}, "product_version": "5.0.0 \u22645.1.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7d50eed9-e332-3c54-a202-aa5d80bc74d1", "vendor": {"name": "smartloli"}}], "isExploited": false}